  <tr><td>Section 20 HAMA</td><td>Hindu parents — father and mother alike</td><td>Civil obligation; quantum flexible; daughter&rsquo;s claim till marriage</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Section 20 DV Act</td><td>Respondent in a domestic relationship</td><td>Child&rsquo;s expenses as part of monetary relief, with interim orders under Section 23</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>The paternity question — handled, not feared</h2>
<p>Denial of paternity is the standard defence, and courts have a standard method. The claim is decided on preponderance of probabilities, as a civil-standard inquiry inside a summary proceeding: evidence of the relationship and cohabitation, hospital and municipal birth records naming the father, school records, photographs, correspondence and financial support already extended all count. Scientific testing is available but not automatic; courts weigh the child&rsquo;s welfare and dignity before directing a DNA test, and treat an unjustified refusal to participate as a circumstance against the refusing party. Two practice realities deserve emphasis: first, the maintenance court&rsquo;s finding on paternity is for the purpose of maintenance and does not conclusively settle status for all purposes; second, interim maintenance does not wait for the paternity trial — courts can and do grant interim relief on a prima facie view, precisely because a child cannot be fed retrospectively.</p>

<h2>Quantum and enforcement</h2>
<p>Once liability is found, the computation is the ordinary one: the child&rsquo;s reasonable needs measured against the payer&rsquo;s means, awarded ordinarily from the date of application. Education costs loom largest in practice — fees, transport, tuition — and courts increasingly provide for them specifically rather than inside a lump monthly figure. Enforcement follows the Section 144 machinery: warrants for levy of the amount due, and, for continued default, detention; arrears applications should be made with the discipline the statute&rsquo;s limitation demands.</p>
<div class="check">
  <p>Claimant&rsquo;s side: file through the mother as next friend, annex the birth record, plead the relationship with dates, and seek interim maintenance at the first hearing.</p>
  <p>Respondent&rsquo;s side: a paternity denial should be accompanied by engagement with the record — bald denial against documents invites adverse findings, and obstruction of testing can do the same.</p>
  <p>Both sides: keep the child&rsquo;s claim conceptually separate from the mother&rsquo;s; the strength or weakness of one does not travel to the other.</p>
</div>
<div class="note">This explainer states general principles for information. Paternity and maintenance disputes turn on their own records, and nothing here is advice in any particular matter.</div>
